                <pb facs="0730" n="618" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg618"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.515/745a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-09-16T15:00:00-04:00">September 16, 1935—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>286. Department desires that in any contacts which you may have with Leith-Ross
                    you adopt friendly attitude and if approached by him on official subjects be
                    cooperative.</p>
                <p>If he inquires whether this Government intends to send a financial attaché, reply
                    as on your own responsibility that you “infer that it will not do so.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
